// "[subject] discards N" ([CR#701.9a]): the DECLARATIVE-SUBJECT discard —
// that player chooses N cards from their hand and discards them
// ([CR#701.9b]). The keyword action as DATA, `Mills`'s twin on the discard
// lane: a `Composite` whose tag is `Discard(who, n)` and whose body is the
// `Each` over the `FromHand` choice of `who`'s hand. The engine batches the
// choice up front and realizes N per-card `Act(Discard)` events (madness
// bites per card, [CR#702.35a]; discard triggers fire once per card).
//
// `who` (Param(0)) rides BOTH the atom and the hand selection's `whose`. The
// template renders the subject context-aware ("Target player discards a
// card."; "Each opponent discards two cards.").
//
// Usage: Discards(It, 1) (the announced player target) / Discards(It, 2).
(
    name: "Discards",
    template: "${0} discards ${1:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect, KeywordAction],
    params: [Reference, Count],
    body: Composite(
        name: Discard,
        body: Each(
            binder: Existing(FromHand(count: Param(1), whose: Param(0))),
            effect: Move(It, Graveyard),
        ),
    ),
)
